==Portuguese==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|roa-ptg|pt}} {{term|lugar|lang=roa-ptg}}, {{term|logar|lang=roa-ptg}}, from {{etyl|la|pt}} {{term|localis|locālis|local|lang=la}}, from {{term|locus||place|lang=la}}, from {{etyl|OL.|pt}} {{term|stlocus|lang=la}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|pt}} {{recons|stel-||to put|lang=ine-pro}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|Portugal}} {{IPA|/lu.ˈɣaɾ/|lang=pt}}
** {{audio|Pt lugar.ogg|Audio}}
* {{a|Paulista}} {{IPA|/lu.ˈgaɾ/|/lu.ˈgaɹ/|lang=pt}}
* {{a|South Brazil}} {{IPA|/lu.ˈgaɾ/|/lu.ˈgaɻ/|lang=pt}}
* {{a|Carioca}} {{IPA|/lu.ˈgaχ/|lang=pt}}

===Noun===
{{pt-noun|m|es}}

# {{l/en|place}} {{gloss|location or position}}
#: {{usex|Não vamos a Camelot, é um '''lugar''' bobo.|t=Let’s not go to Camelot, it’s a silly '''place'''.|lang=pt}}
# {{l/en|available}} {{l/en|room}}
#: {{usex|Há '''lugar''' para cinco pessoas neste carro.|t=There is '''room''' for five people in this car.|lang=pt}}
# {{l/en|place}} {{gloss|position within a rank}}
#: {{usex|Quem fica em primeiro '''lugar''' ganha medalha de ouro.|t=He who gets first '''place''' earns gold medals.|lang=pt}}
# {{uncountable|lang=pt}} {{l/en|opportunity}} {{gloss|chance for advancement, progress or profit}}
#: {{usex|Não dê '''lugar''' à corrupção.|t=Leave no '''space''' for corruption.|lang=pt}}
#: {{usex|Não tive '''lugar''' para terminar o serviço.|t=I didn’t have '''an opportunity''' to finish the job.|lang=pt}}
# a {{l/en|reserved}} or {{l/en|available}} {{l/en|seat}}
#: {{usex|Teremos que comer em outro lugar, aqui não há mais '''lugares'''.|t=We will have to eat elsewhere, there are no '''seats left''' here.|lang=pt}}
# a {{l/en|position}} in a {{l/en|book}}, {{l/en|song}} or {{l/en|film}}
#: {{usex|Parei de ler o livro naquele '''lugar'''.|t=I stopped reading the book on that '''spot'''.|lang=pt}}

